; DOMAIN: stable-homotopy-theory [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: The stable homotopy category is obtained from spaces by inverting suspension: a spectrum E is a sequence {E_n} with structure maps S^1 ∧ E_n -> E_{n+1}, and stable homotopy groups pi_n^s(X)=colim_k pi_{n+k}(S^k X) are the suspension-stable homotopy classes. The Freudenthal suspension theorem guarantees pi_{n+k}(S^k X) stabilizes for k > n+1. The category is triangulated, symmetric monoidal under smash product, with sphere spectrum S as unit; [X,Y] becomes a graded abelian group. The Adams spectral sequence Ext_{A}^{s,t}(H^*Y, H^*X) => pi_{t-s}(Y)^_p computes stable stems from mod-p cohomology as a module over the Steenrod algebra A.
; Structure: (spectrum = sequence E_n with S^1∧E_n->E_{n+1}) (pi_n^s = colim suspension) (Freudenthal stabilization k>n+1) (triangulated + smash-monoidal, unit = sphere spectrum) (Adams SS Ext_A => stable stems p-completed).
; Result: stable homotopy linearizes unstable homotopy into a triangulated monoidal category where cohomology theories are representable (Brown representability) and the sphere spectrum's homotopy = the stable stems.
; Bridge: genesis_bott_periodicity (KU/KO are spectra, Bott = periodicity of the K-theory spectrum) + genesis_k_theory (K-theory is a representable cohomology theory = spectrum) + genesis_homology (generalized homology theories = smashing with a spectrum, Brown representability) + genesis_spectral_sequence (Adams SS computes stable stems).
(= (suspension-spectrum $X) (sequence (smash (sphere 1) $X_n) $X_next))
(= (stable-homotopy-group $X $n) (colim-suspension (homotopy-group (iterated-suspension $X) $n)))
(= (freudenthal-stable $X $n $k) (iso (homotopy-group (suspension-k $X $k) (plus $n $k)) (stable-homotopy-group $X $n)))
(= (smash-unit) (sphere-spectrum))
(= (adams-ss $X $Y) (converges (ext-steenrod (mod-p-cohomology $Y) (mod-p-cohomology $X)) (p-completed-stable $Y)))